      "summary": "18 DEPARTMENT OF ADMINISTRATIVE AND FINANCIAL SERVICES \n \n125 MAINE REVENUE SERVICES \n \nChapter 302: SALES TO GOVERNMENTAL AGENCIES AND EXEMPT \nORGANIZATIONS\n \n \n \n \nSUMMARY:  Establishes administrative rules regarding tax-exempt sales and explains \nthe circumstances under which a retailer or service provider will be relieved of its burden \nof proving that sales to an entity described in 36 M.R.S. §§ 1760 or 2557, including an \nagency or instrumentality of the federal government or of the State of Maine, are exempt \nfrom Maine sales, or use, or service provider tax. \n \n  \nSECTION 1.  Exempt sales generally; burden of proof \n 1. Generally Sales and Use Tax.  Sales to certain organizations and governmental \nagencies are exempt from sales and use tax pursuant to 36 M.R.S. § 1760.  Pursuant to 36 \nM.R.S. § 1760-C, an exemption provided by 36 M.R.S. § 1760 to a person based upon its \ncharitable, nonprofit , or other public purposes applies only if the property or service \npurchased is intended to be used by the person primarily in the activity identified by the \nparticular exemption.  The burden of proving a sale is to an organization that is exempt \nunder 36 M.R.S. § 1760 is on the person making the sale.  The retailer is relieved of this \nburden of proof if it satisfies the provisions of this rule.  \n 2. Certain purchases subject to tax.  Pursuant to 36 M.R.S. § 1760- C, an \nexemption provided by 36 M.R.S. § 1760 to a person based upon its charitable, nonprofit, \nor other public purposes applies only if the property or taxable service purchased is \nintended to be used by the person primarily in the activity identified by the particular \nexemption.  If property or taxable services that were purchased exempt are used primarily \nin an activity or  activities not identified by the particular exemption, use tax liability \naccrues.   \nAn exemption based on charitable, nonprofit, or other public purposes  does not \napply to any purchase for use by an exempt organization in it",
      "title": "302 Sales to Government Agencies and Exempt Organizations (PDF)"
